<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 16.7 bln levs of 1-wk, 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 16.7 bln levs of 1-wk, 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on Wednesday sold two discount T-bill issues with maturities of one and four weeks, yielding 3.63 percent and 17.54 percent to maturity, respectively, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Bids were received for a total 17.172 billion levs of paper, but the ministry approved bids for only 16.742 billion levs worth.</p>
<p>Details of the issues follow: </p>
<p> Issue number		  BG 3011897009     BG3011997007</p>
<p> Term			    one week	     four weeks</p>
<p> Auction date		  January 22, 1997   January 22, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date		    January 22, 1997   January 22, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		 January 29, 1997   February 19, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		 11,782.1 mln levs  5,390 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.50 pct	    85.07 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 11,362.1 mln levs  5,380 mln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.50 pct	    85.08 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity	3.63 pct	    17.54 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
